I don't want to stop now

33
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,200
I want to laugh and laugh

34
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,200
I want to laugh

35
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,200
Are you not supposed to try when you have no chance?

36
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,200
Uh, what's that?

37
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,200
Trying when you don't have a chance

38
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,200
Are you talking about Kyoko?

39
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:23,200
And am I supposed to go for someone else

40
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,200
Just because I do have a chance?

41
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,200
I mean, I get it, I do

42
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,200
If a bunch of hot girls said

43
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,200
Let's play beach volleyball together

44
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,200
Whoops, I'm doing right into you

45
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,200
Obviously I would be down for that

46
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,200
And of course I want hot girls my age

47
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,200
To come cheer for us when we play

48
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,200
But it's different!

49
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,200
Tommy says these are two different things!

50
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,200
We know

51
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,200
We're all well aware that it's just part of who you are, bud

52
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:51,200
I think we knew it from the very first day you joined

53
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,200
Oh, great

54
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,200
He's on the volleyball team too

55
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,200
Better be sure not to make eye contact

56
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,200
Oh, great

57
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:21,200
Wow

58
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,200
Ah

59
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,200
Will

60
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:31,200
Will!

61
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,200
Will?

62
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,200
Will what?

63
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,200
Will you please marry me?

64
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:47,720
Yeah, no.

65
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:55,860
It's so good.

66
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:58,000
I love the proposal at first sight incident.

67
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,640
Perfectly expresses who Tanaka is.

68
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:01,660
It does.

69
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:02,060
Yeah.

70
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,100
I'm getting restless thinking about tomorrow.

71
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,420
I'm going to go for a walk.

72
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,940
Is he going to be okay?

73
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:15,580
I'm just kind of worried that he may be obsessed to the point of turning into a stalker.

74
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,060
I don't think he'd go that far.

75
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:22,540
He's extremely perceptive about people's feelings, and if Kyoko ever asked him to back off for real, I'm sure he would.

76
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,200
Then he'd disappear.

77
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,720
I know we like to call him an idiot, but he's actually a pretty amazing guy.

78
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:33,120
He's so simple and so devoted.

79
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:37,720
I think it's really hard to be that way.

80
00:04:37,720 --> 00:05:06,280
Relief server Tadashi Yamaguchi is making use of his time on the court.

81
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,580
They got us, you guys!

82
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:09,900
Quiet down, Atsumu!

83
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:10,640
Huh?

84
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,040
I'm so sorry.

85
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:13,540
See?

86
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,640
Look what you've done.

87
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,880
One more time!

88
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,200
That's it!

89
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,200
Well done!

90
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:36,260
Couldn't he see he wouldn't get to it before he hit the wall?

91
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:38,380
Even if he did, he couldn't return it.

92
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:44,340
I'm pretty sure the only thing in his mind was the fact that the ball still hadn't actually made contact with the ground.

93
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:50,380
It's like, I don't know, like he doesn't have the time or brain space to just stop.

94
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,760
Stupid ball!

95
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,300
Clumsy receive, Phil!

96
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:08,040
The ball is headed back over the net!

97
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:09,960
We still have a chance.

98
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,960
Kageyama!

99
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,960
Let's go!

100
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:13,540
Let's go!

101
00:06:17,260 --> 00:06:17,960
Finish it!

102
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,800
I got it!

103
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,960
And the block's into Anna Bills!

104
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:31,780
Thanks, Kageyama!

105
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:32,580
Sure.

106
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:35,160
You played like an ace, Asahi!

107
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:36,120
Thanks a lot!

108
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,500
Yeah, well, that's his job.

109
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,840
Everyone's totally on their game right now.

110
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,340
Okay, so that can't be legal, right?

111
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:50,440
Well, neither the player nor the ball went into a Narazaki's court.

112
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:51,060
It's fine.

113
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,900
Hey, where the hell did you just go?

114
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,500
You missed your boy Tadashi in action!

115
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:57,840
You dropping a damn deuce?

116
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,360
I needed to rescue Tadashi!

117
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,940
And those stares are brutal.

118
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:04,420
Man, I hit it right there, number one!

119
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:07,060
I was trying to aim for number five like Coke said!

120
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,320
It's fine.

121
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:12,260
And Karasuno manages to get to set point first!

122
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:15,820
If they miss this chance, the next server will be Atsumumiya.

123
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:20,020
And I'm pretty sure Karasuno does not want to have to deal with that guy again.

124
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:22,460
That kid is a menace!

125
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:29,060
We have a chance.

126
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:32,620
We definitely have a chance!

127
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:40,040
Oh, and he is shut down!

128
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:43,740
The spike was rejected by middle blocker Rintaro Suna!

129
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,760
Nice kill, Rintaro!

130
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:47,800
That's me.

131
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,220
That was a bit short.

132
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:52,340
Nah, I totally thought we were gonna make that one work just fine!

133
00:07:52,340 --> 00:08:02,280
If that were me down there, I'd be so pissed off, I'd be spiking the ball right into the net at this point.

134
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,280
He's actually aware of that?

135
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:14,600
Please, don't let him serve more than once.

136
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:18,280
Aim your serves at the number five.

137
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:21,760
He's been out there the entire game and hasn't been making any great plays.

138
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:25,160
If we're gonna drag them down, it's gotta start with him.

139
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:32,740
It's coming for me.

140
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,840
I'm used to everyone aiming for me.

141
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:43,400
Come at me!

142
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,020
Bring it on!

143
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:52,540
Yeah, there we go!

144
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:53,380
No way!

145
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:58,800
Am I just, like, a total loser today?

146
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:09,460
Come on, guys.

147
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,680
You were their blockers to you.

148
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:19,920
Frankly, this is not my favorite thing, but...

149
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:25,140
And Sawa Muna scores from the back row!

150
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:28,140
Nice one, nice one, guys!

151
00:09:28,140 --> 00:09:32,640
Karasuno has managed to limit the dangerous Atsumomiya to just one serve!

152
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,720
Not too bad, guys.

153
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,700
Nice kill, Daichi!

154
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:38,880
Thanks!

155
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:45,300
And now, Karasuno is at set point yet again!

156
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,100
Nice bump!

157
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:58,720
Oh, that looked like a brand new play.

158
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,920
Why try it with his team facing set point?

159
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:01,700
Ha ha!

160
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:02,800
I love it!

161
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,040
Keep it up, young man!

162
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,640
Chance ball!

163
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:08,800
He's fast.

164
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:12,640
They're getting their blocks in place!

165
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,800
Even faster than before!

166
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:18,100
Dammit, man!

167
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,120
It'll take more than that to break my bro!

168
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,440
Yes, ma'am!

169
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:23,720
Seek quick!

170
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:29,560
We'll stop it!

171
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:35,240
Did I hit that one a little hard?

172
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,360
Dammit!

173
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,980
What have I even done today?

174
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:42,680
Left side!

175
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:43,480
Tanaka!

176
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:47,400
What have I accomplished?

177
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:51,760
Three blockers!

178
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,260
He's overreacting.

179
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:09,980
Only not really.

180
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,460
Inarizaki's blocking is stubborn.

181
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,020
And that brings with it a sense of desperation.

182
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:18,940
Add that to the stress of having all the servers go after him,

183
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:21,180
and a single mistake will be all it takes.

184
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:25,560
That's enough to make a guy feel like he's doing everything wrong.

185
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:51,260
Hojitsu Middle School!

186
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,960
Name's Ryunosuke Tanaka!

187
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:53,580
Sup!

188
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,600
What's with his hair?

189
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:57,440
I sense a strong will in him.

190
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:59,200
He's not going to bow down to anybody.

191
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,860
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

192
00:12:00,860 --> 00:12:04,580
Kurasuno hasn't been performing that well lately.

193
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,660
But in my heart, it's still a powerhouse.

194
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:10,040
Kurakawa from Hisa Middle School.

195
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,920
Asahi from Sekodai.

196
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,260
Both awesome spikers I saw in tournaments and heard were here.

197
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:18,100
And from my ear, Nishinoya's here too.

198
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:20,760
But I don't know.

199
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,220
The reality's not that exciting.

200
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,880
Other teams need the gym today, so we're going to be outside.

201
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:27,660
Right!

202
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,480
This again?

203
00:12:29,660 --> 00:12:30,100
Why?

204
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,540
Can we go complain to someone?

205
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,540
Hey, it's way better than last year,

206
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,060
and there's plenty of work we can do practicing outside.

207
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:38,880
What a bunch of damn pushovers.

208
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,460
Thank you very much, guys.

209
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,820
Thanks for the game!

210
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:50,560
They weren't as tough as I thought they'd be.

211
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,820
I mean, that was barely even a warm-up.

212
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,640
I didn't even break a sweat.

213
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:57,480
I'll shut them up!

214
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:58,740
How's that?

215
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:00,140
Oh, real easy.

216
00:13:00,380 --> 00:13:02,780
I'll just go over when no one's looking and give them a...

217
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:04,360
Just give them the business!

218
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:05,760
Let it go!

219
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:08,080
We should just be grateful they're playing us at all.

220
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:11,620
And besides, today was our first match with the new team.

221
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:12,720
We were a mess.

222
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,960
So you're just going to let them say all that about us?

223
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,320
You don't think that's weak?

224
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,240
Just have to win.

225
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:25,040
It may not be easy, but it's very simple.

226
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,420
Get used to it.

227
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,780
This happens a lot.

228
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:32,020
Guys are always whispering behind our backs at official matches.

229
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,720
Yeah, they call us...

230
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,900
Karasino's Falling Champions.

231
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,080
Clipped Crows.

232
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:44,140
Well, their eyes aren't laughing.

233
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:51,920
All my life, I've seen all my mentors as adults, even if they were only a year older than me.

234
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,580
But I have a different kind of respect for these guys.

235
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,080
It's like somehow I just know...

236
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,280
These guys are strong.

237
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:06,060
Oh, wow!

238
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:07,340
What happened to your head, man?

239
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:08,600
I...

240
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:11,820
I just thought I should do something to get myself psyched up again.

241
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:13,960
Let me touch it!

242
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:14,520
Get out of me!

243
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:32,760
Lucky!

244
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:34,900
Yeah, you got that right.

245
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:36,860
Also, you owe me some pudding.

246
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:38,740
Not the kind that's sold in three packs.

247
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:39,080
Huh?

248
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:39,900
That wasn't me!

249
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,840
They're tied up again!

250
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,520
Can Karasino find a way to pull out of this, Phil?

251
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:48,540
Did the Orange Team do something especially bad?

252
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:51,060
That wasn't just a one-time miss.

253
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:55,440
It's more like the pressure from Inarizaki's blocks is building steadily.

254
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,460
And that miss proved it.

255
00:14:58,100 --> 00:14:59,340
Snap out of it, Tanaka!

256
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:00,700
That was a good shot!

257
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:01,780
Yeah, okay!

258
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:04,740
Damn it!

259
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:06,400
Push through this, Baldi!

260
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,300
You can do it!

261
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:09,200
Now's the time to show the world your stuff!

262
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,680
He'll be fine.

263
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:12,780
Still Tanaka.

264
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:16,420
He's certainly always been pretty tough during matches.

265
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:20,680
And of all us second years, with everything that's happened to the team,

266
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:23,840
no matter what, the one who always stayed...

267
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:26,460
was Tanaka.

268
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:28,840
Let's go!

269
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:31,520
Come on.

270
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,640
This is the part where you're supposed to clam up

271
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,840
and stop being able to look your teammates in the eye.

272
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:42,740
I got it!

273
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:44,740
The setter got first contact.

274
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,540
